# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Large inputs and intermediates. None of these belong in the repository; the
# README and docs/REPRODUCIBILITY.md explain how to obtain or rebuild each one.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# SWAN-SF v1.2 tarballs, 5.74 GB. Download from the Harvard Dataverse
# (DOI 10.7910/DVN/EBCFKM) into raw_data/.
raw_data/

# Extracted features: data/features/ is 241 MB of chunks and the two merged
# files are another 190 MB. Rebuild with:
#   python -m solarflare features   (needs raw_data/, hours)
#   python -m solarflare audit      (merges the chunks, about four minutes)
data/

# Superseded report draft kept only for local reference.
reference/

# Microsoft Word lock files.
~$*

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Committed deliberately, recorded here so the choice is visible:
#   models/            all seven pipelines, 28 MB, largest file 14 MB. Keeping
#                      them means a fresh clone reproduces the full
#                      seven-candidate table without retraining.
#   results/           every frozen metric, prediction file and log, 4.8 MB.
#   figures/           the report's figures, 1.9 MB.
#   dashboard/         the static demo and its generated JSON.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

